= Saxony: our vote against Buck

Wilhelm Buck's Social Democratic minority government lives on our ten votes in the Landtag. Its interior minister, Richard Lipinski, uses the Saxon police like any other: against strikers, against our meetings, against the unemployed. The party has put its conditions to the SPD: control committees on prices, workers' defence against the leagues, an end to police action against the workers. Buck has not met them.

Our motion of no confidence in Lipinski is on the order paper. The bourgeois parties will vote with us for their own reasons.

